0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2","ipc",{"law":{"id":"ipc","title":"Indian Penal Code, 1860","short":"IPC","year":"1860 · historical / saved matters","kind":"Act","status":"historical","summary":"The former general penal code. Study it for historical incidents, older judgments, and the transition to the BNS.","url":"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/2263","caution":"Repealed prospectively from 1 July 2024, subject to savings. Do not use old section numbers without checking the applicable law.","topics":["1.7","1.4"],"sections":[{"number":"34","title":"Common intention","text":"Addresses acts done by several persons in furtherance of common intention. Compare BNS section 3(5), while checking the exact facts and statutory wording."},{"number":"120B","title":"Punishment of criminal conspiracy","text":"Read with the definition of criminal conspiracy in section 120A. The BNS reorganizes this framework in section 61; do not infer identical coverage from the topic label."},{"number":"354C–354D","title":"Voyeurism and stalking","text":"The former provisions addressed specified private-image and repeated-contact or monitoring conduct. Broadly compare BNS sections 77 and 78, including their definitions and exceptions."},{"number":"384","title":"Extortion","text":"The former punishment provision for extortion, read with section 383. Compare BNS section 308 and the facts of a coercive digital payment demand."},{"number":"406","title":"Criminal breach of trust","text":"The former punishment provision, read with section 405. Compare BNS section 316 and examine entrustment, dishonesty, and the property involved."},{"number":"419","title":"Cheating by personation","text":"Read with section 416. Broadly compare BNS section 319(2), and distinguish the computer-resource-specific offence in IT Act section 66D."},{"number":"420","title":"Cheating and dishonestly inducing delivery","text":"Read with the definition in section 415. Broadly compare BNS section 318(4); dishonest inducement and the other elements remain necessary."},{"number":"463–465","title":"Forgery and punishment","text":"The former definition and punishment framework. Compare BNS section 336, including its express treatment of false electronic records and the relevant punishment subsection."},{"number":"468","title":"Forgery for purpose of cheating","text":"The former aggravated forgery provision. Broadly compare BNS section 336(3), checking the intended use and statutory elements."},{"number":"471","title":"Using a forged document as genuine","text":"The former provision for fraudulent or dishonest use. Compare BNS section 340(2), read with the relevant definition of a forged document or electronic record."},{"number":"499–500","title":"Defamation","text":"The former definition, exceptions, and punishment. Compare BNS section 356, which reorganizes the framework rather than merely changing the number."},{"number":"503, 506, 509","title":"Intimidation and insulting modesty","text":"The former criminal-intimidation and modesty-related provisions. Broadly compare BNS sections 351 and 79, applying the exact threatened conduct and statutory exceptions."}]}}]],[["$","script","script-0",{"src":"/_next/static/chunks/0h8rqv9vsrp80.js","async":true}]],["$","$L3",null,{"children":["$","$4",null,{"name":"Next.MetadataOutlet","children":"$@5"}]}]]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
